    <item>
      <title>CUR 2.0 Overview &amp; Architecture</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/CUDOS-with-AmazonQuick/03-cur2-foundation/01-cur2-overview/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/CUDOS-with-AmazonQuick/03-cur2-foundation/01-cur2-overview/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;aws-badge &#34;&gt;CUR 2.0&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;span class=&#34;aws-badge &#34;&gt;AWS Data Exports&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;span class=&#34;aws-badge &#34;&gt;Amazon S3&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;aws-duration&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;far fa-clock&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Estimated duration:&lt;/strong&gt; 10 mins&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;cur-20-overview--architecture&#34;&gt;CUR 2.0 Overview &amp;amp; Architecture&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-is-cur-20&#34;&gt;What is CUR 2.0?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;CUR 2.0 is a detailed AWS cost and usage dataset delivered through AWS Data Exports. It can include billing, line-item, product, pricing, reservation, Savings Plans, resource-tag, and Cost Category information.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The exact fields populated depend on the charge type and service.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;collection-architecture&#34;&gt;Collection architecture&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Single workshop AWS account&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        │&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        ├── Source: AWS Billing / Data Exports&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        │&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        └── Destination: Data Collection&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;                ├── S3 bucket&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;                ├── Glue database/tables&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;                └── Athena query layer&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;aws-callout callout-note&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;p&gt;📸 &lt;strong&gt;Screenshot placeholder — &lt;code&gt;03-01-cur2-architecture.png&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Prerequisites &amp; AWS Identity Check</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/CUDOS-with-AmazonQuick/03-cur2-foundation/02-prerequisites-identity/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/CUDOS-with-AmazonQuick/03-cur2-foundation/02-prerequisites-identity/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;aws-badge &#34;&gt;AWS STS&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;span class=&#34;aws-badge &#34;&gt;AWS Billing&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;span class=&#34;aws-badge &#34;&gt;AWS CloudFormation&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;aws-duration&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;far fa-clock&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Estimated duration:&lt;/strong&gt; 5 mins&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;prerequisites--aws-identity-check&#34;&gt;Prerequisites &amp;amp; AWS Identity Check&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;step-1--get-the-account-id&#34;&gt;Step 1 — Get the Account ID&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-powershell&#34; data-lang=&#34;powershell&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;aws sts get-caller-identity `&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  --profile &amp;lt;PROFILE&amp;gt; `&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  --query Account `&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  --output text&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Copy the value into your private workshop notes as:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;lt;ACCOUNT_ID&amp;gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;aws-callout callout-note&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;p&gt;📸 &lt;strong&gt;Screenshot placeholder — &lt;code&gt;03-02-account-id.png&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Capture the successful account ID lookup. Redact the value before publishing if desired.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Replace this block with the real screenshot after completing the step.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Deploy the CUR 2.0 Data Export Foundation</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/CUDOS-with-AmazonQuick/03-cur2-foundation/03-deploy-data-export/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/CUDOS-with-AmazonQuick/03-cur2-foundation/03-deploy-data-export/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;aws-badge &#34;&gt;AWS CloudFormation&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;span class=&#34;aws-badge &#34;&gt;AWS Data Exports&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;span class=&#34;aws-badge &#34;&gt;CUR 2.0&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;aws-duration&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;far fa-clock&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Estimated duration:&lt;/strong&gt; 15–20 mins&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;deploy-the-cur-20-data-export-foundation&#34;&gt;Deploy the CUR 2.0 Data Export Foundation&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Official guide:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guidance/latest/cloud-intelligence-dashboards/data-exports.html&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;step-1--launch-the-destination-stack&#34;&gt;Step 1 — Launch the Destination stack&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Open the official guide above.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Go to &lt;strong&gt;Deployment → Step 1 of 3 — Create Destination for Data Exports&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Choose &lt;strong&gt;Launch Stack&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;When CloudFormation opens, confirm the Region is &lt;strong&gt;Asia Pacific (Sydney)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;aws-callout callout-note&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;p&gt;📸 &lt;strong&gt;Screenshot placeholder — &lt;code&gt;03-05-launch-destination-stack.png&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Capture the official Launch Stack link or the pre-populated CloudFormation create-stack page.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Validate Data Export &amp; S3 Delivery</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/CUDOS-with-AmazonQuick/03-cur2-foundation/04-validate-delivery/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/CUDOS-with-AmazonQuick/03-cur2-foundation/04-validate-delivery/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;aws-badge &#34;&gt;AWS Data Exports&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;span class=&#34;aws-badge &#34;&gt;Amazon S3&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;span class=&#34;aws-badge &#34;&gt;CUR 2.0&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;aws-duration&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;far fa-clock&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Estimated duration:&lt;/strong&gt; 10 mins &amp;#43; delivery wait&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;validate-data-export--s3-delivery&#34;&gt;Validate Data Export &amp;amp; S3 Delivery&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;step-1--verify-the-export-exists&#34;&gt;Step 1 — Verify the export exists&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Open:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Billing and Cost Management → Data Exports&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Find the CUR 2.0 export created by the stack.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Check:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Export type is CUR 2.0.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Destination is the workshop collection bucket.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Export configuration looks healthy.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;aws-callout callout-note&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;p&gt;📸 &lt;strong&gt;Screenshot placeholder — &lt;code&gt;03-10-cur2-export.png&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Capture the CUR 2.0 export entry and destination. Do not fabricate an export name.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
